==Serbo-Croatian==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|sla-pro|sh}} *rędъ.. Cognate with Bulgarian {{m|bg|радея||care for}}, Russian {{m|ru|радеть||care for}}. Non-Slavic cognates include Ossetian {{m|os|рад||order}}, Sanskrit {{m|sa|राध्यते}}, {{m|sa|राधति}} and {{m|sa|राध्नोति||tr=rādhnóti|succeed}}, Gothic {{m|got|𐌲𐌰𐍂𐌴𐌳𐌰𐌽|tr=garedan}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/rǎːditi/|lang=sh}}
* {{hyphenation|ra|di|ti|lang=sh}}

===Verb===
{{sh-verb|head=ráditi|a=impf}}

# {{lb|sh|intransitive}} to [[work]]
#: {{ux|sh|Ne mogu doći sutra, '''radit ću''' do kasno u noć!|I can't come tomorrow, I'll be working late into the night}}
# {{lb|sh|transitive}} to [[do]], [[act]]
#: {{ux|sh|Što '''radiš''' sutra?|What are you doing tomorrow?}}
# {{lb|sh|reflexive}} to [[concern]], [[be]] about
#: {{ux|sh|O čemu se ovdje '''radi'''?|What is this about?|lit=What is this here about?}}

